# What gets uploaded to Vercel and bundled into the Python function.
#
# This is an allowlist, not a list of things to leave out: the first rule
# ignores everything, and each "!" line adds one thing back. Anything new --
# a new top-level folder, a new pile of research under data/ -- stays out of
# the deployment unless someone adds it here on purpose. That is deliberate.
# A denylist would have to be updated every time the repository grows, and
# would silently ship whatever nobody remembered to add.
#
# scripts/tests/docs/evals/.github are covered by the first rule.

/*
!app.py
!pyproject.toml
!vercel.json
!deadbot
!web

# data/ carries ~165 MB of research material. The running site never opens
# any of it -- it serves from PostgreSQL, and deadbot/storage.py refuses to
# start any other way. Only the handful of small files the request path
# actually reads are added back: the top-level *.json config files, plus the
# editorial and coverage sets. data/raw and data/canonical stay out.
!data
data/*
!data/*.json
!data/editorial
!data/coverage
